WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.920
Do we finally know what Luffy's real dream
is?

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:10.650
Not to become pirate king, but the one that
Oda-sensei has only hinted at in his flashback

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.900
with Sabo and Ace.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:19.050
The exact same dream that also Roger had and
that inspired people like Crocus, Shanks and

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:24.620
Rayleigh to put all their faith in our rubbery
boy to change the world.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:30.730
Well, I think chapter 1049 of One Piece really
seems to suggest so.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.590
At the climax of the epic battle between Luffy
and Kaido, both of them attacking with what

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:41.820
seems like their last, ultimate techniques,
the emperor asks Luffy what kind of world

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.430
he wants to make if he actually is strong
enough to change it.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:53.600
And in a series of 3 absolutely incredible
double spreads, Luffy replies that he wants

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.930
to make a world in which his friends can eat
and drink as much as they wish.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:05.379
Argh, I can't even begin to explain the sort
of goosebumps that this gave me.

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:12.000
Now, why do I think does this answer not only
make a ton of sense, but more importantly

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.760
also wonderfully embodies the main theme and
message of One Piece as a story?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.440
There's a lot packed into this little statement.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:29.220
One big theory that I heard being thrown around
a while ago, is that Luffy's real dream might

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:35.610
be to have a giant banquet with all his friends,
based on the fact that the end of every major

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.979
arc and victory for the crew, Luffy would
celebrate with a feast.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:46.299
Which, honestly was really close, but did
not quite hit the mark.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:53.640
Because a banquet would imply that Luffy's
biggest desire is having one giant event with

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.170
all his friends laughing and feasting together.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:02.890
Which I absolutely DO think will happen, but
it doesn't quite address the main theme of

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.600
the story, Freedom.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.959
The fact that Luffy wants to make a world
where everyone can eat as much as they want,

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:14.750
friends and food, the two things that he loves
the most in this world, implies that he wants

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:19.510
them to have the freedom live the happiest
life he can imagine.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:26.280
To me, it's the most Luffy way of saying that
he wants to liberate the world.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.760
It takes Luffy's biggest character quirk,
eating like there is no tomorrow, and connecting

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.270
it to the central moral message of One Piece,
which I just find absolutely beautiful.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:44.010
The banquets that Luffy had so far always
are a celebration of life among equals that

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.080
now are free to do whatever they like.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.260
Eat, drink, sing, dance.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:56.000
Because as we know, at this point, Luffy is
basically friends with everyone in the world,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.920
except those who stand in the way of everyone
else's happiness.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.300
In a world, where most people live in poverty
and despair, ruled by a small group of people

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:11.470
that have all the wealth and luxury, I would
argue that means LUffy's goal is to take down

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.420
the world nobles and free the world.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:22.569
Which ironically is exactly what Kaido's goal
is, whose flashback I'm pumped to discuss

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:24.180
in a moment of course.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.060
And so even more awesomely, is awesomely a
word?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.580
Hm, now it is.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:34.790
Even more awesomely, the theme of eating and
drinking as much as one likes not only references

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:41.599
the story as a whole, but of course also connects
wonderfully to the themes of Wano in particular.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:45.540
A country that is starving and has no clean
water to drink.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:51.129
An arc that literally started with Luffy being
gifted the little bit of Tama's rice that

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:52.500
she had.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:59.920
He shouts that dream at the climax of the
raid on onigashima, where Kaido has been holding

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:06.780
a yearly banquet with all the food and drinks
anyone could want, but only for his men and

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.580
those with power.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:15.510
Even though Luffy and Kaido share the same
goal in a way, freeing the world, Kaido has

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:21.309
taken the wrong path to get there, becoming
what he hated the most in the process.

00:04:21.309 --> 00:04:26.800
Don't you find it ironic, that we see Kaido
literally declaring war on the nobles that

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.779
took away his freedom and that of the people
he loved by creating a de-facto system of

00:04:32.779 --> 00:04:36.300
world nobles inside wano itself?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.900
That is Kaido's big flaw as a character, that
in the end only Luffy will be able to make

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.050
him see.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.810
It's very similar to Big Mom I feel, now that
I think about it.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:53.909
Because she has created an ACTUAL country
made out of food, also pretty much based on

00:04:53.909 --> 00:04:58.939
Luffy's dream, only that here the people are
of course not really free to do whatever they

00:04:58.939 --> 00:05:04.460
want and live a happy life, though, let's
be real, it's a lot better than Wano.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:10.639
Two of the Yonko have basically started where
Luffy did, only that where Kaido and Big Mom

00:05:10.639 --> 00:05:15.520
lost there course somewhere along the way
and turned into villains, Luffy will be the

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:24.580
one who actually succeeds in making this dream
a reality, WITHOUT becoming the bad guy in

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:25.580
the process.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.949
That's what always has made Luffy special
and why I love this chapter and the reveal

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:33.849
of Luffy's actual dream so much.

00:05:33.849 --> 00:05:38.809
Did you notice how young Big Mom is very similar
to young Luffy?

00:05:38.809 --> 00:05:40.620
Genuinely kind and caring.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:45.979
Or how young Kaido in this chapter basically
looks like a young Luffy with horns?

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:50.899
And actually, since we're on the topic now,
let me share my thoughts on Kaido's flashback

00:05:50.899 --> 00:05:52.210
that we got in this chapter.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:58.950
Ah, okay so as you will notice, I absolutely
LOVED the overall story for Kaido and how

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:04.710
he became who he is today and I will go into
detail here in just a moment, but I do have

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.759
to get this one thing off my chest first.

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:13.699
If this is everything we are going to get
for his past, that would be way way too short

00:06:13.699 --> 00:06:15.860
for me personally.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:21.740
This is the final villain of not only the
longest arc in all of One Piece, but also

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.069
the entire Yonko Saga past the time skip.

00:06:25.069 --> 00:06:31.909
Kaido has gotten a ton of absolutely next
level character development during Onigashima,

00:06:31.909 --> 00:06:38.240
but I just really really want to see more
details and more interactions from his past.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.309
Like at LEAST an entire chapter or two.

00:06:41.309 --> 00:06:42.309
Or three.

00:06:42.309 --> 00:06:43.309
Or four.

00:06:43.309 --> 00:06:46.570
I want to see more of Kaido interacting with
Big mom and whitebeard.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:52.969
I do get that Oda-sensei is probably saving
a lot of that for when he actually reveals

00:06:52.969 --> 00:06:58.929
Rocks and his past, but still I think Kaido
is interesting and important to the story

00:06:58.929 --> 00:07:00.050
NOW.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:07.839
So if this is it, not long enough for me personally
haha.

00:07:07.839 --> 00:07:09.300
I want more.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:14.069
However that being said, what gives me a lot
of hope that we will still see a lot more

00:07:14.069 --> 00:07:21.310
from Kaido's past, is the fact that we still
don't know why he was experimented on, how

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:28.020
he recruited the rest of his men, how he learned
about Joy Boy and so on and so forth.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.909
So truly fingers crossed for more.

00:07:30.909 --> 00:07:37.029
The flashback that we DID get so far though,
content wise was just so so good.

00:07:37.029 --> 00:07:44.089
I love the fact that Kaido is from a kingdom
that's called Vodka, given that he's a pretty

00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:45.249
bad alcoholic.

00:07:45.249 --> 00:07:52.550
How he made a name for himself as his countries
strongest warrior, only to be sold off to

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:57.279
the marines by the king for the chance to
get more power by getting access to the Reverie.

00:07:57.279 --> 00:08:04.770
He comes from an island that did war and plundering
to raise enough money for the heavenly tribute,

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.929
which is basically protection money a country
has to pay to the world government to not

00:08:09.929 --> 00:08:16.709
be attacked by them.

00:08:16.709 --> 00:08:19.939
This explains a lot of Kaido's character traits.

00:08:19.939 --> 00:08:25.219
He has known nothing but war, ever since he
was a little kid.

00:08:25.219 --> 00:08:30.469
He has learned to hate the world government
as they are responsible for his childhood

00:08:30.469 --> 00:08:33.659
and being sold and betrayed.

00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:38.889
I absolutely love that Oda-sensei baited us
by saying that Kaido was captured and executed

00:08:38.889 --> 00:08:44.680
a bunch of times by the Marines, but as it
turns out, most of the time he just escaped

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:49.310
and let himself be recaptured whenever he
became hungry.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:54.519
Which is not only the most hilarious explanation
for the strongest creature being captured

00:08:54.519 --> 00:09:00.940
that often, but it also ties in nicely with
the food theme of Luffy's dream again.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:07.069
Another really interesting detail I found
was once again big moms interaction with Kaido.

00:09:07.069 --> 00:09:12.960
It really seems like these two used to have
a much much closer relationship than we originally

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:13.960
thought.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:18.680
Inline is almost eating like a big sister
here and is shocked to find out that Kaido

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:23.329
once again vanished after Rocks was defeated
by Garp and Roger.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:29.839
Again, we still don't know how this all played
out, but it sounds like at least these two

00:09:29.839 --> 00:09:34.829
were pretty close even after whatever went
down on god valley.

00:09:34.829 --> 00:09:41.290
But in a way, the most important reveal in
this chapter to me, was something that I had

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:46.590
already been speculating for quite a while
now.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:52.100
Kaido basically confirms that he has been
trying to bring about the return of Joy Boy.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:57.149
And while King thought that it would be Kaido
himself, Kaido clearly was waiting for the

00:09:57.149 --> 00:09:59.129
one who could defeat him.

00:09:59.129 --> 00:10:04.689
Which is why he was so so disappointed at
the beginning that Luffy couldn't defeat him,

00:10:04.689 --> 00:10:10.240
only that Luffy came back not once, not twice,
but three times.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.579
Each time stronger and more determined before.

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:22.980
And the fact that Kaido remembers this conversation
with King, to me really shows that he is almost

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:30.100
relieved that Luffy has delivered such a massive
blow and has been able to push him this far.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:35.350
The flame clouds have vanished, which has
finally triggered Momo into fully summoning

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:36.660
clouds of his own.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.510
Now, the big question is of course.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:42.990
Is Kaido defeated or not?

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:48.120
While all of this clearly sets up our expectations
for Kaido being defeated here and Luffy having

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:54.320
run out of steam too, I personally would like
to think that this fight isn't over.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:58.209
Luffy has come back a number of times in this
fight already, but Kaido hasn't had to pull

00:10:58.209 --> 00:11:01.240
off a full comeback even once so far.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:06.709
I still don't believe that we have seen his
awakened form yet and I would honestly like

00:11:06.709 --> 00:11:09.500
this battle to continue on for a bit longer.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.629
I feel like Kaido will stand back up.

00:11:13.629 --> 00:11:17.939
However it doesn't necessarily have to be
against Luffy.

00:11:17.939 --> 00:11:25.160
I think the last panel shows us, that Kaido
has realized that Luffy is Joyboy and is acknowledging

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.460
his power.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:29.660
Luffy has overcome him in this moment.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:36.209
But I would absolutely love to see Kaido getting
back up to defend Luffy against government

00:11:36.209 --> 00:11:42.269
forces or blackbeard or whoever might try
to take Luffy out while they still have the

00:11:42.269 --> 00:11:43.269
chance.

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:49.310
Kaido defending JoyBoy and inheriting his
own will to free the world onto Luffy would

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:56.699
be a fantastic redemption arc for his character,
that for whatever reason I really want to

00:11:56.699 --> 00:11:58.490
see for Kaido.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:02.339
If you want to know why, you really cant ignore
this analysis of Kaido I've done.

00:12:02.339 --> 00:12:06.119
And if you've enjoyed this video, why not
subscribe to the channel for more.

